a be all over it  so there are people who want to say yes  to you the people at my business I pay  them but they would work for me even if  I didn't pay them because they love  this business stands for what does your  company stand for there has to be  something special you don't want people  only to come for you because you're  paying them well or you're paying them  something there has to be a greater  purpose so know that there are people  out there and it starts with you  identify that passion identify the  purpose of what you're doing in your  company and there are definitely highly  talented skilled people who want to  partner up and work with you  the second part of should you accept  people who you ask to join you but they  said no should you accept them back into  your business later once you become  successful this is a no brainer for me  why would you want somebody in your  business who said no to you before who  didn't believe in what you were doing  and said no and now what they suddenly  believe in your company that's BS I  don't want people on my team who do not  want to help entrepreneurs who don't  believe in what we're all about  because those people won't last if  somebody's there just for the money or  just for the opportunity they're not  gonna last you want the people who  strongly believe in your core and they  would join you if you're at the startup  stage or if you're well established if  somebody says no to you because they  don't believe in what you're all about  then you should never bring that person  on board you could be friends you know  it doesn't have to be personal I've I've  hired and fired my best friend than my  business and we're still friends so you  don't have to make it personal but that  guy is never gonna come back and work in  my business and if people say no I don't  want to join you they should never be  allowed to join you you missed out and  now that we're successful you want to  come back on board not happening you  